 "title": "CSS Specificity",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "CSS Specificity"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "CSS Specificity"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "CSS specificity is an algorithm that determines which style declaration is ultimately applied to an element."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "If two or more CSS rules point to the same element, the declaration with the highest specificity will \"win\", and\nthat style will be applied to the HTML element."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Look at the following examples:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<html>\n<head>\n  <style>\n    p {color: red;}\n\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<p>Hello World!</p>\n\n</body>\n\n  </html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_specificity_el"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Now, look at next example:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<html>\n<head>\n  <style>\n    .test {color: green;}\n\n    p {color: red;}\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<p class=\"test\">Hello World!</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_specificity_class"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Now, look at next example:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<html>\n<head>\n  <style>\n    #demo {color: blue;}\n\n  .test {color: green;}\n    p {color: red;}\n\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<p id=\"demo\" class=\"test\">Hello\n  World!</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_specificity_id"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Now, look at next example:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<html>\n<head>\n  <style>\n    #demo {color: blue;}\n\n  .test {color: green;}\n    p {color: red;}\n\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<p id=\"demo\" class=\"test\"\n  style=\"color: pink;\">Hello World!</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_specificity_inline"
  }
 ]
